program	errors/ref_field_nested_in_tuple.saw
triple	arm64-apple-darwin
twin	same
expect	error
build	refused	Parse error at 12:21: field `pair` of `Both` may not be a reference: its type `(Int, &Int)` names a reference (`&Int`), and references in Saw are PARAMETERS ONLY — a reference borrows storage for the duration of one call and may not escape it (designs 88/106; the Law of Exclusivity is statically sound only because every live reference belongs to a call still on the stack). A field outlives every call that could have created the reference, so the pointer it holds outlives the storage it names. Store the value instead (drop the `&`: `&Int` becomes `Int`), or — to hand out storage this type already owns — declare a `borrows` accessor (`... borrows -> &var Int` with `lend`, design 141), which lends the place for a window rather than letting a pointer out
